  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set for the dependency-graph analysis. Key findings that shaped the selection:\n\n- **Detection logic**: Spring Boot's `Log4J2LoggingSystem.Factory` (in `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java`) gates activation on `ClassUtils.isPresent(\"org.apache.logging.log4j.core.impl.Log4jContextFactory\", ...)` \u2014 a class in `log4j-core`, not `log4j-api` or `log4j-to-slf4j`. `LoggingSystem.java` / `LoggingSystemFactory.java` show how this factory is discovered via `spring.factories`.\n- **Bridge modules**: `log4j-to-slf4j` (routes Log4j2 API calls to SLF4J) and `log4j-slf4j-impl`/`log4j-slf4j2-impl` (routes SLF4J calls to Log4j2) are mutually exclusive bridges \u2014 `Log4jLoggerFactory.java` and `SLF4JLoggerContextFactory.java` throw `LoggingException`/`IllegalStateException` if both are on the classpath simultaneously.\n- **Dependency chain**: `spring-boot-starter-logging` pulls `log4j-to-slf4j` (so any Log4j2 API calls route to Logback via SLF4J), while `spring-boot-starter-log4j2` pulls `log4j-slf4j2-impl` + `log4j-core` + `log4j-jul` and must exclude `spring-boot-starter-logging` to avoid the bridge collision.\n- **log4j-bom** confirms the modern artifact set (`log4j-api`, `log4j-core`, `log4j-to-slf4j`, `log4j-slf4j-impl`, `log4j-slf4j2-impl`, `log4j-spring-boot`) as of 2.20.0.\n- Included `log4j-spring-boot`'s `Log4j2SpringBootLoggingSystem` since it subclasses Spring Boot's `Log4J2LoggingSystem` directly and is the concrete integration point Log4j2 itself ships for Spring Boot.",
